& [StableWriteSurface] is available
  + [thread_start] accepts sandbox workspace-write, approvalPolicy never, exact cwd, ephemeral true, and developer instructions
  + [turn_start] accepts a workspaceWrite SandboxPolicy with networkAccess false, excludeSlashTmp, excludeTmpdirEnvVar, and additional writableRoots
  + [turn_start] accepts exact cwd, approvalPolicy, input, and outputSchema
  + [turn_interrupt] exists as an explicit request
  + [finding] is no modified llama.cpp or Codex fork is required for a bounded workspace-write experiment

& [ObservableItems] are useful but not preventive proof
  + [commandExecution] exposes item identity, command string, best-effort commandActions, cwd, status, aggregated output, duration, exit code, and process identity when available
  + [commandActions] currently classify read, listFiles, search, or unknown and explicitly describe parsing as best effort
  + [fileChange] exposes item identity, status, and path/diff/kind changes
  + [output_deltas] expose command and file-change progress
  + [finding] is command strings and file-change events can be accounted and faulted but do not constitute a pre-execution policy engine
  + [finding] is an item/started or interrupt response cannot prove that no filesystem mutation preceded observation

& [ApprovalBoundary] is closed for the proposed profile
  + [server_requests] include commandExecution requestApproval, fileChange requestApproval, permission requests, MCP elicitation, and user input
  + [profile] uses approvalPolicy never and treats every server request as a fault
  + [reason] is the manager has no Phase3B authority to grant escalation

& [SandboxBoundary] has explicit limitations
  + [workspaceWrite] is the only selected mutable sandbox profile
  + [network] can be false
  + [writableRoots] can be an empty additional set
  + [temporary_directories] can be excluded from writable scope on platforms supporting those flags
  + [windows_warning] windows/worldWritableWarning reports directories that cannot be protected by the sandbox and includes failedScan, samplePaths, and extraCount
  + [requirement] is failed scan or any relevant world-writable warning fails before the turn
  + [requirement] is physical tests must challenge writes to principal workspace, Git common dir, parent, temp, network, symlink or reparse escape, and allowed candidate path
  + [nonclaim] is schema shape alone does not prove operating-system sandbox enforcement

& [ExcludedInterfaces] are material
  + [standalone_command_exec] is not used
  + [unsandboxed_shell_field] is explicitly outside the thread sandbox contract and is forbidden
  + [dynamic_tools] remain experimental and unused
  + [persistent_threads] remain unused
  + [approvals_reviewer] is not used to manufacture new authority

& [MissingStableControl] constrains the solution
  + [prewrite_path_allowlist] is not present as a stable App Server field
  + [command_allowlist] is not present as a stable turn field
  + [transactional_rollback] is not present
  + [authoritative_post_state] is not supplied by streamed model events
  + [finding] is the disposable worktree is the preventive containment unit; allowed-path enforcement is a Phase3C post-state gate unless an OS policy is separately added and proven

& [ActivationBlockers] are concrete
  + [blocker_1] is prove workspaceWrite physical containment on the active Windows host including world-writable warning behavior
  + [blocker_2] is define exact mutable event grammar and bounded command accounting
  + [blocker_3] is define immutable pre-state handoff and Phase3C post-state sealer contract
  + [blocker_4] is define which model-run commands are observed versus which supervisor-run tests count as proof
  + [blocker_5] is define abort, child cleanup, dirty disposable worktree handling, and operator recovery without granting cleanup authority
